# Issue #1188 R1188-U23 (owner, 2026-10-08, a strict requirement): every
# regular code file in js/, ts/, rust/ (and scripts/, packages/) is
# human-readable multi-line code. scripts/check-readable-code.mjs fails a
# tracked code file that is packed (more than 160 characters per line on
# average) or holds a line of more than 300 characters of code, unless it is
# listed here. Only real distribution bundles belong here, each with its reason. A path ending in / covers every
# file under it. An exemption that no longer covers an unreadable file fails
# the gate, so this list only shrinks.
#
# The built web bundles (js/*.bundle.js, js/app.js) are git-ignored build
# output, so the gate never sees them and they need no row.

readable-code-exemption js/vendor/tree-sitter/web-tree-sitter.mjs
  reason "Vendored distribution build of the web-tree-sitter package, committed as upstream published it (js/vendor/tree-sitter/provenance.lino); its Emscripten glue holds one line of about 4,100 characters. Reformatting it would make it differ from the published artifact its provenance names."
